  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "ydcbmiq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO INFRASTRUCTURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Infrastructure is broadly divided into Economic Infrastructure (Transport, Power, Telecom) and Social Infrastructure (Education, Health, Sanitation).",
        "Economic infrastructure directly supports productive activities, whereas social infrastructure indirectly boosts economy by building human capital.",
        "Major infrastructure initiatives in India include the National Infrastructure Pipeline (NIP) and the PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan for multimodal connectivity.",
        "In India's power sector, thermal power remains the dominant source of electricity generation, though renewable energy capacity is expanding rapidly.",
        "Major bottlenecks in Indian infrastructure development include high financial stress, land acquisition delays, environmental clearance issues, and DISCOM losses."
      ],
      "id": "apohapm"
    },
